Supreme People's Court

Notice on Printing and Issuing the
Implementation Measures for the Expert Appraisal Name List System of People's Courts

Fa Fa [2004] No. 6

To the High People's Courts of all provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government; the Military Court of the People's Liberation Army; and the Production and Construction Corps Branch of the High People's Court of the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region:

The Implementation Measures for the Expert Appraisal Name List System of People's Courts are the supporting document of the Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on the Administration of Commissioned Forensic Appraisal by People's Courts (Fa Shi [2002] No. 8). They are hereby printed and issued to you. Please forward them to the people's courts within your respective jurisdictions, and earnestly organize their implementation to further standardize the forensic appraisal work of the people's courts.

February 9, 2004

Implementation Measures for the Expert Appraisal Name List System of People's Courts

Chapter I General Provisions

Article 1 These Measures are formulated in accordance with relevant laws, regulations, and the Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on the Administration of Commissioned Forensic Appraisal by People's Courts, for the purposes of making full use of social appraisal resources, ensuring the smooth progress of forensic appraisal work in the people's courts, standardizing the expert appraisal name list system of the people's courts, and improving the quality and efficiency of commissioned and organized appraisal work.

Article 2 The expert appraisal name list system of the people's courts refers to the process by which the people's courts, after pre-approval review, approval, and public announcement procedures, include social appraisers (including natural persons and legal persons) who voluntarily accept commissioned appraisal from the people's courts in the appraisal name list of the court at the corresponding level. Where appraisal is needed in cases heard by the people's courts, the case is uniformly transferred to a specialized body, which is responsible for commissioning or organizing the appraisal. The appraiser is determined by a combination of respecting the parties' choice and random selection from the name list, and the specialized body is responsible for coordinating and supervising the appraisal work.

Article 3 The establishment and implementation of the expert appraisal name list system of the people's courts shall follow the principles of territorial management, voluntary application, merit-based selection, resource sharing, openness, and fairness.

Article 4 The forensic appraisal body of a people's court shall be responsible for the establishment and implementation of the expert appraisal name list system, and shall manage the name list dynamically based on the circumstances of commissioned and organized appraisal.

A basic people's court that does not have a forensic appraisal body or does not need to establish its own name list shall designate a specialized body and assign specialized personnel to use the name list of the higher people's court in accordance with these Measures, and shall be responsible for commissioning and organizing appraisal work.

Chapter II Establishment of the Expert Appraisal Name List

Article 5 Each high people's court may, based on the needs of trial work, formulate a plan for the number of levels of appraisal name lists to be established within its jurisdiction and the number of appraisers in each level of the name list, and submit it to the Supreme People's Court for approval before implementation.

Article 6 Any social appraisal, testing, or evaluation unit that voluntarily applies for inclusion in the expert appraisal name list of the people's court shall fill in the "Application for Inclusion in the Name List of Commissioned Forensic Appraisal Institutions of the People's Court" and submit the following materials:

(1) Duplicate and copy of the business license for an enterprise or social organization legal person;
(2) Duplicate and copy of the professional qualification certificate;
(3) List of professional and technical personnel, their professional qualifications, and main achievements;
(4) Annual inspection documents and copies thereof;
(5) Other necessary documents and materials.

Article 7 Any professional or technical person who voluntarily applies for inclusion in the expert appraisal name list of the people's court on an individual basis shall fill in the "Application for Inclusion in the Name List of Forensic Appraisal Experts of the People's Court" and submit the following materials:

(1) Duplicate and copy of the professional qualification certificate;
(2) Evidence of main achievements and copies thereof;
(3) Other necessary documents and materials.

Article 8 The forensic appraisal body of a people's court shall conduct a comprehensive review of the appraiser making the application, focusing on their professional qualifications, industry reputation, work performance, and whether there have been any violations of laws or discipline.

Article 9 To avoid duplicate registration, an appraiser shall submit an application for inclusion in the name list to the people's court in the place where they are located. A higher people's court may select appraisers from the name list approved and submitted by a lower people's court, provided that the consent of the appraiser is obtained, and after approval, the appraiser shall be included in the name list of the higher people's court.

Article 10 The expert appraisal name lists of the people's courts shall be uniformly compiled by the Supreme People's Court and announced in the People's Court Daily. The high people's courts shall assist in handling matters related to the announcement.

Where appraisers are deleted from or added to the appraisal name list in accordance with these Measures, the matter shall be reported level by level to the Supreme People's Court for arrangement of the announcement.

Article 11 Appraisers included in the name list shall submit to the annual review conducted by the forensic appraisal body of the relevant people's court and provide the following materials:

(1) Annual work report and industry annual inspection status;
(2) Changes in professional and technical personnel;
(3) Updates to instruments and equipment;
(4) Other changes and materials required to be submitted.

If any changes in the annual review require announcement, the forensic appraisal body of the relevant people's court shall report them level by level to the Supreme People's Court.

Article 12 An appraiser who voluntarily withdraws from the name list shall submit written materials to the forensic appraisal body of the people's court. Upon approval by the forensic appraisal body of the higher people's court, the appraiser shall be removed from the name list. Failure to participate in the annual review shall be deemed as automatic withdrawal.

Chapter III Application of the Expert Appraisal Name List

Article 13 After accepting a case referred for appraisal from its own court or a lower court, the forensic appraisal body of a people's court shall assign one or two appraisal supervisors to be responsible for coordinating and supervising the appraisal work, and assisting in resolving relevant problems. However, they shall not interfere with the appraiser's independent decision-making regarding the appraisal conclusion.

Article 14 The main duties of an appraisal supervisor are:

(1) Organizing the parties to negotiate or randomly selecting an appraiser;
(2) Handling the formalities for commissioning the appraisal;
(3) Implementing the withdrawal of appraisers as required;
(4) Coordinating with and assisting the appraiser in inspecting the site and collecting appraisal materials;
(5) Coordinating and monitoring the progress of the appraisal;
(6) Reviewing the appraisal documents and, where necessary, organizing relevant personnel to hear opinions;
(7) Notifying and urging the appraiser to appear in court according to law.

Article 15 The appraisal supervisor shall preside over the participation of the parties in jointly selecting the appraiser. If a party fails to appear without justifiable cause within the specified time, the appraisal supervisor shall randomly select the appraiser.

Where the law specifies the appraiser, or where the appraisal of evidence in litigation may harm the interests of the state, the collective, or a third party, the parties shall not select the appraiser through negotiation.

Article 16 Random selection of an appraiser refers to the use of random methods such as drawing lots or shaking numbers to determine the appraiser from among those in the same appraisal category in the appraisal name list.

Article 17 If an appraiser selected through unanimous agreement of the parties is not included in the appraisal name list, the appraisal supervisor shall review the appraiser. If significant problems are found, the supervisor shall preside over the parties to re-select an appraiser.

Article 18 If the specialty involved in the forensic appraisal is not included in the appraisal name list, the forensic appraisal body of the people's court may select, from relevant social specialties, a commissioned unit or professional to conduct the appraisal on a merit basis. If the selected appraiser needs to be included in the appraisal name list, the procedures specified in these Measures shall be followed.

Article 19 Where a commissioned appraisal needs to use the name list of a court in another locality or a higher court, contact shall be made with the forensic appraisal body of the people's court that established that name list, the appraisal case shall be transferred, or relevant information during the coordination and supervision of the appraisal process shall be promptly communicated to such body for necessary assistance.

Chapter IV Related Responsibilities

Article 20 An appraiser included in the expert appraisal name list of the people's court shall bear responsibility for the appraisal conclusion. Under any of the following circumstances, the forensic appraisal body of the people's court may, as the case may be, order correction, suspend the commissioning, recommend that the industry competent authority of the appraiser impose sanctions, or announce in the People's Court Daily the removal from the name list:

(1) Accepting forensic appraisal business not in accordance with the provisions of these Measures;
(2) Privately meeting with a party during the appraisal process;
(3) Violating the appraisal procedures or failing to perform duties responsibly, resulting in a serious error in the appraisal conclusion;
(4) Failing to fulfill the obligation of confidentiality;
(5) Failing to complete the appraisal within the prescribed time limit without justifiable cause;
(6) Failing to fulfill obligations such as appearing in court without special reasons.

Article 21 If an appraiser violates laws, regulations, or relevant provisions, or causes serious consequences due to intentional fault resulting in an erroneous appraisal conclusion, legal liability shall be pursued according to law.

Article 22 If an appraisal supervisor of a people's court, in the process of commissioning forensic appraisal and coordinating and supervising the appraisal, violates provisions and causes consequences, responsibility shall be pursued by reference to the Measures for Pursuing Liability for Illegal Adjudication (Trial) and the Measures for Imposing Disciplinary Sanctions in Adjudication (Trial) of the People's Courts.

Chapter V Supplementary Provisions

Article 23 These Measures shall be interpreted by the Supreme People's Court.

Article 24 These Measures shall come into force on the date of their promulgation.
